# Controls what reaches the Docker daemon as build context — defense in
# depth against .env ever reaching the daemon at all, and meaningfully
# faster builds (state/ alone carries tens of MB of research data).
#
# Does NOT exclude engine/ — dashboard/Dockerfile's explicit
# `COPY engine/__init__.py engine/attribution.py engine/config.py` needs
# those files present in the build context. This file controls what's SENT
# to the daemon; the Dockerfile's selective COPY controls what actually
# lands IN the image. The two are complementary, not redundant.

.git/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.env
.env.example
state/
reports/
exports/
backtest/
logs/
tests/
deploy/
.claude/
